{"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"title":"Explanation","generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The Snapshot Pattern","type":"heading","anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via "},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"State(observer:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" packs, "},{"code":"State.apply(_:to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" unpacks."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" equality checking.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accessor checks ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"_modify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accessor (used by ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through ","type":"text"},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cross-slice observation isolation.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro generates a separate ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" class for each ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property. A view reading ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.items","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" won’t re-render when only ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.ui","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates the observer class tree and "},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Explicit equality guards (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }"},{"text":") are unnecessary. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" already checks equality on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"text":". Unconditional assignment is safe.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Note"},{"text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","type":"heading","anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" warns if "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means "},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Reducer Weight","type":"heading","anchor":"Reducer-Weight","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatch the result back as an action."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Effect Threading","type":"heading","anchor":"Effect-Threading","level":2},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"text":". Blocking calls (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Process.waitUntilExit()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"code":"terminationHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"code":"waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Task.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", async file I\/O instead of "},{"code":"Data(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","kind":"symbol","title":"Effect","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Async work with cancellation metadata declared before the store starts it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","kind":"symbol","title":"PersistencePlugin","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxObservable":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxObservable","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","kind":"symbol","title":"SwiduxObservable","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxObservable","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Bridges a value-type state struct to an ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"code